WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:03.131
Okay, welcome back to Nagarjuna.

00:00:03.131 --> 00:00:05.850
[laughs] [unclear].

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:08.663
And we're going to go to chapter 17,

00:00:09.933 --> 00:00:12.992
which is, I don't know,
this chapter is weird

00:00:12.992 --> 00:00:16.210
because you can understand it.

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:19.430
So I was thinking Nagarjuna's
sitting there and he's like

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:22.540
let me write one chapter
that they can understand.

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:26.921
And so, I don't know, you're
probably going to get bored now.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:29.470
But here, let's go to it.

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:34.470
Now, it's worthwhile to say
that you might ask yourself

00:00:35.915 --> 00:00:39.990
why did he write a chapter
that we can understand now?

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:44.460
You know, after sixteen
un-understandable chapters,

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:47.135
why does he suddenly
give us an easy chapter?

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.930
I think trying to guess
why Nagarjuna does stuff

00:00:52.930 --> 00:00:56.293
is like a very interesting way
to spend a couple of hours.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:59.973
All right, so here's
the name of the chapter.

00:01:01.271 --> 00:01:03.790
LAS BRTAGS PA ZHES BYA BA

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:06.540
And I don't know if you
noticed, Tim, for example,

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:08.923
but he changed the spelling of BRTAGS PA.

00:01:10.907 --> 00:01:14.160
Somebody changed the spelling,
probably Choney Lama.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:19.080
And instead of saying an
investigation of karma,

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:24.080
he says let's investigate karma.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:27.860
It's interesting, he made a verb.

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:29.467
Let's investigate karma.

00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:32.278
So this chapter is called
"The Investigation of Karma".

00:01:32.278 --> 00:01:36.801
All right, here we go,
let's go to the first verse.

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:43.432
Do you want to read, Tim?

00:01:43.432 --> 00:01:45.781
,BDAG NYID LEGS PAR SDOM PA DANG,

00:01:45.781 --> 00:01:49.889
,GZHAN LA PHAN 'DOGS BYAMS SEMS GANG,

00:01:51.156 --> 00:01:54.988
,DE CHOS DE NI 'DI GZHAN DU,

00:01:54.988 --> 00:01:57.177
,'BRAS BU DAG GI SA BON YIN,

00:01:57.177 --> 00:01:59.102
- Good, okay. BDAG NYID?

00:02:00.386 --> 00:02:01.219
- [Tim] Self.

00:02:01.219 --> 00:02:03.643
- Yeah, but it's touchy

00:02:03.643 --> 00:02:07.618
because he said BDAG NYID, me myself.

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:09.680
Where is he going to go?

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:12.690
When Nagarjuna says me myself, you're like

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:14.220
where are you going next?

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:16.974
Then he says SDOM PA -

00:02:16.974 --> 00:02:20.270
- [Woman] Vow.
- Vow, but the verb?

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:22.670
Control yourself.

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:25.645
The verb for SDOM PA
means to control yourself.

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:28.970
So LEGS PA, LEGS SO LEGS SO.

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:32.520
'Well', to control yourself 'carefully',

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:37.073
to control yourself carefully.

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:42.042
And really it's BYAMS PA.

00:02:43.585 --> 00:02:45.260
- [Woman] Love.
- Love, it's love.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:47.184
BYAMS SEMS means thoughts of love.

00:02:47.184 --> 00:02:49.660
PHAN 'DOGS GZHAN means to help others.

00:02:49.660 --> 00:02:52.950
Thoughts of love where
you want to help others.

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:57.177
Now, all throughout these verses we go

00:02:57.177 --> 00:03:00.180
BDAG NYID LEGS PAR SDOM PA DANG.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:02.010
By the way when you go to the monastery

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:03.819
and hear the kids memorizing,

00:03:03.819 --> 00:03:07.594
BDAG NYID LEGS PAR SDOM PA DANG

00:03:07.594 --> 00:03:10.411
GZHAN LA PHAN 'DOGS BYAMS SEMS GANG

00:03:10.411 --> 00:03:11.736
DE CHOS DE NI

00:03:11.736 --> 00:03:13.520
No, Nagarjuna says don't say that,

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:17.820
say DE... CHOS, don't read it DE CHOS.

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:19.120
What's the difference?

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:22.633
DE... CHOS

00:03:22.633 --> 00:03:26.810
That's CHOS, that's Dharma.

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:30.860
It's powerful, he says DE... CHOS.

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:32.835
What's DE?

00:03:32.835 --> 00:03:35.107
SDOM PA and BYAMS PA

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:38.730
Control yourself from hurting others,

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:41.955
be nice to others, and love others.

00:03:41.955 --> 00:03:46.810
DE, don't say DE CHOS, say DE... CHOS.

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:48.470
That's Dharma.

00:03:48.470 --> 00:03:51.754
Yeah, and Choney Lama
adds a DKAR PO there.

00:03:53.504 --> 00:03:56.260
DKAR PO, you have a DKAR PO shoes on.

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:58.383
- [Student] White.
- Yeah, white.

00:03:59.708 --> 00:04:02.874
That's pure Dharma.

00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:08.453
Choney Lama says, "That's
dharma as white as snow!"

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:14.313
Picture?
[all laughing]

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:19.760
That's Dharma DKAR PO.

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:21.950
Choney Lama says, "Nagarjuna said

00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:24.810
"that's Dharma, that's what Dharma is,

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:27.100
loving other people and not hurting them."

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:30.748
But Choney Lama says, "And
that's as white as snow."

00:04:30.748 --> 00:04:33.280
All right, GZHAN LA PHAN DE CHOS.

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:36.430
Now, what happens if you
do that kind of thing?

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:38.603
You get 'BRAS BU.

00:04:38.603 --> 00:04:39.436
[student responding indistinctly]

00:04:39.436 --> 00:04:42.400
You get results, and then.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.110
Okay, here's $100.

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:50.800
Еhe Tibetan translator
put, okay Christina,

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:53.225
he put in the dual.

00:04:54.531 --> 00:04:58.956
When he wrote fruits or results,

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:03.153
he used the ending which
means the two results.

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:05.274
Why?

00:05:05.274 --> 00:05:08.148
It's at the end of the
third line if you can guess.

00:05:08.148 --> 00:05:12.398
[students responding indistinctly]

00:05:13.723 --> 00:05:18.673
TSE 'DI, TSE 'DI TSE GZHAN

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:21.633
Life, life.

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:26.617
Life, TSE 'DI LA -- in this life

00:05:27.451 --> 00:05:29.640
and in your future lives.

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:32.741
For $100, how did the Yoga Sutra say that?

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:38.510
[student responding indistinctly]

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:42.340
In the first chapter of the Yoga Sutra,

00:05:42.340 --> 00:05:44.576
they say that exact same thing.

00:05:49.023 --> 00:05:53.950
@

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:56.410
Experienced in this life
and in the next life,

00:05:56.410 --> 00:05:59.918
seen in this life and
seen in the next life.

00:05:59.918 --> 00:06:01.159
All right.

00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:06.890
Anyway, the results of
controlling yourself

00:06:06.890 --> 00:06:11.680
from hurting others and from
thoughts of love towards others

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:15.024
is the SA BON of 'BRAS BU,

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:18.050
the two 'BRAS BUs,

00:06:18.050 --> 00:06:19.600
in this life and your next life,

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:21.760
in the future lives, okay, got it?

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:23.810
There's nothing difficult
about that verse.

00:06:23.810 --> 00:06:26.768
I don't know, Nagarjuna's losing it.

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:30.420
It's just a simple truth.

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:31.577
Then you're like suspicious,

00:06:31.577 --> 00:06:34.910
you're like, well, where's he going now?

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:37.163
Here we go, next verse.

00:06:40.366 --> 00:06:43.374
,DRANG SRONG MCHOG GIS LAS RNAMS NI,

00:06:43.374 --> 00:06:45.499
,SEMS PA DANG NI BSAM PAR GSUNGS,

00:06:45.499 --> 00:06:47.673
,LAS DE BDAG GI BYE BRAG NI,

00:06:47.673 --> 00:06:50.594
,RNAMS PA DU MAR YONGS SU BSGRAGS,

00:06:50.594 --> 00:06:52.976
DRANG SRONG CHEN PO means the great sage,

00:06:52.976 --> 00:06:55.790
DRANG SRONG is sidhi,

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:58.600
okay, the great yogi.

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:00.747
Who's the great, the ultimate yogi?

00:07:00.747 --> 00:07:02.431
- [Woman] Buddha.
- The Buddha.

00:07:02.431 --> 00:07:06.950
Because sometimes he's called DRANG
SRONG CHEN PO -- the ultimate yogi.

00:07:06.950 --> 00:07:09.660
You could got to use that in YSI somehow.

00:07:09.660 --> 00:07:12.740
The ultimate yogi means the Buddha.

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:16.095
He said you can divide all karma,

00:07:16.095 --> 00:07:21.095
LAS, into SEMS PA and BSAM PA.

00:07:21.312 --> 00:07:25.043
[student responding indistinctly]

00:07:25.043 --> 00:07:27.213
BSAM, past tense.

00:07:28.374 --> 00:07:31.643
[student responding indistinctly]

00:07:31.643 --> 00:07:33.484
LAS LAS 'JIG RTEN SNA TSOGS SKYES

00:07:33.484 --> 00:07:36.217
DE NI SEMS PA DANG DES BYAS

00:07:37.072 --> 00:07:37.912
Opening-

00:07:37.912 --> 00:07:39.820
[student responding indistinctly]

00:07:39.820 --> 00:07:42.520
Yeah, thoughts and what they motivate.

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:44.560
So thoughts and thought.

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:48.695
Thinking and thought,
thinking and thunked.

00:07:48.695 --> 00:07:50.500
Thinking and thunked.

00:07:50.500 --> 00:07:53.490
That's a new verb, Pachi.

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:55.450
SEMS PA DANG NI BSAM PAR GSUNGS.

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:58.140
SEMS PA means intention,

00:07:58.140 --> 00:08:00.970
and BSAM PA means what you intended to do,

00:08:00.970 --> 00:08:02.970
which means what you say and what you do.

00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:05.470
So he's covered how many?

00:08:05.470 --> 00:08:07.620
He's actually covered
three kinds of karma.

00:08:08.569 --> 00:08:12.120
SEMS PA -- mental karma,

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:14.530
and then BSAM PA,

00:08:14.530 --> 00:08:16.100
what you say and what you do.

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:18.710
And that's all the kinds
of karma there are.

00:08:18.710 --> 00:08:21.530
So the DRANG SRONG MCHOG,
the great, the ultimate yogi,

00:08:21.530 --> 00:08:25.887
he said -- GSUNGS, "You
could divide all karma into

00:08:25.887 --> 00:08:30.204
intending to do something and then
the things you intended to do.

00:08:31.086 --> 00:08:34.932
Intention and intended.

00:08:34.932 --> 00:08:36.372
LAS DE BDAG GI BYE BRAG NI

00:08:36.372 --> 00:08:38.134
Now, if you want to divide those up,

00:08:38.134 --> 00:08:40.217
SPYI BYE BRAG, right, here it is.

00:08:40.217 --> 00:08:43.497
If you want to divide
up those kinds of karma,

00:08:43.497 --> 00:08:47.998
DU MAR -- there's billions.

00:08:47.998 --> 00:08:49.090
Just forget it.

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:54.006
YONGS SU BSGRAGS means
you can find described

00:08:54.006 --> 00:08:56.600
hundreds, and hundreds,
and hundreds of divisions.

00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:59.020
Basically those two:

00:08:59.020 --> 00:09:02.700
intention and what you
intended to say or do.

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:04.258
Okay, got it?

00:09:07.010 --> 00:09:10.330
Let's do some Sanskrit.

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:14.240
And I thought it would be nice to know

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:17.210
the words for intention

00:09:17.210 --> 00:09:20.160
and what you intended to do or say.

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:21.423
So here we go.

00:09:22.820 --> 00:09:27.420
Intention, or what you're thinking to do,

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:28.930
is called cetanā (chetana).

00:09:28.930 --> 00:09:30.894
Chetana, say chetana.

00:09:30.894 --> 00:09:31.727
[students repeat]

00:09:31.727 --> 00:09:34.010
Yeah, the Tibetan is SEMS PA

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:36.353
which is the definition
of karma in Tibetan.

00:09:37.955 --> 00:09:40.040
@SEMS PA

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:44.150
Karma is thinking to do something.

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:47.743
Raw karma, raw karma is intention.

00:09:47.743 --> 00:09:50.800
It comes from the root
√cit which means to think,

00:09:50.800 --> 00:09:53.430
which literally means to shine.

00:09:53.430 --> 00:09:55.970
And in ancient times it was believed

00:09:55.970 --> 00:09:58.513
that thinking illuminated the world.

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:02.853
If you ever died, the world would go dark.

00:10:03.810 --> 00:10:04.660
See what I mean?

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:07.240
That's why the world is called "loka",

00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:10.883
which means lucid, same root.

00:10:10.883 --> 00:10:13.361
%Roach, also roach.

00:10:13.361 --> 00:10:18.361
To shine from within so the
world is illuminated by the mind

00:10:18.370 --> 00:10:20.530
so the mind is called √cit

00:10:20.530 --> 00:10:22.680
which means √cit which means...

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:25.150
here it's called √kweit.

00:10:25.150 --> 00:10:26.830
It used to be "kshit"

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:28.860
then it goes to @

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:29.900
then it comes "kshwit"

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:33.963
then is becomes "kweit",
and then it becomes white.

00:10:35.350 --> 00:10:38.951
Or wheat because that becomes
white when you grind it.

00:10:38.951 --> 00:10:42.610
So wheat means the white grain.

00:10:42.610 --> 00:10:46.190
So the mind illuminates the world,

00:10:46.190 --> 00:10:51.179
and that's why the mind
is called the whitener.

00:10:51.179 --> 00:10:54.700
[laughs] Okay, got it? √cit.

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:58.029
And if you know Russian, I mean
there are many, many roots.

00:10:58.029 --> 00:10:59.437
Schitat (считать) means to consider,

00:10:59.437 --> 00:11:01.637
chitat (читать) means to read,

00:11:01.637 --> 00:11:05.288
schitayu (считаю) --
I consider, like that.

00:11:05.288 --> 00:11:07.121
Okay, or I read, okay.

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:12.405
Now, the opposite, cetayitvā (chetayitva)

00:11:12.405 --> 00:11:14.250
is BSAM PA in Tibetan.

00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:16.450
What you thought, which means

00:11:16.450 --> 00:11:18.240
what you're doing and what you're saying.

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:20.560
The thunked, say.

00:11:20.560 --> 00:11:24.365
And that's just a simple
passive form, right,

00:11:24.365 --> 00:11:26.490
with the "ya", chetayitva.

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:27.780
That which you are thinking.

00:11:27.780 --> 00:11:29.600
The "tva"

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:34.583
came into English as -tion,
like locomotion or action.

00:11:36.450 --> 00:11:38.480
Makes it a noun.

00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:39.890
Cool, we finished our...

00:11:39.890 --> 00:11:41.980
just remember "chit" means to think,

00:11:41.980 --> 00:11:45.047
and it's tied up with illumination,

00:11:45.047 --> 00:11:48.620
"shchit" means shine.

00:11:48.620 --> 00:11:50.068
Shine came from that.

00:11:50.068 --> 00:11:52.653
All right, here we go.

00:11:54.240 --> 00:11:55.440
Next verse.

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:58.410
So what's unusual about
this chapter so far?

00:11:58.410 --> 00:12:00.990
Two verses in a row we understood

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:03.080
what the heck he's talking about.

00:12:03.080 --> 00:12:06.350
And he doesn't seem to
have brought up emptiness.

00:12:06.350 --> 00:12:10.630
And I assert that this is the first verse

00:12:10.630 --> 00:12:12.730
he ever didn't bring it up,
and he's got two in a row,

00:12:12.730 --> 00:12:13.770
which is really suspicious.

00:12:13.770 --> 00:12:16.160
I mean this is where university scholars

00:12:16.160 --> 00:12:19.320
say somebody added this chapter [laughs].

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:20.507
Which I don't think is true,

00:12:20.507 --> 00:12:23.060
but anyway it's a little suspicious.

00:12:23.060 --> 00:12:24.035
Okay, here we go,

00:12:24.035 --> 00:12:26.076
,DE LA LAS GANG SEMS PA ZHES,

00:12:26.076 --> 00:12:28.660
,GSUNGS PA DE NI YID KYIR 'DOD,

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:31.643
Universally miscarved.

00:12:31.643 --> 00:12:33.767
,BSAMS PA ZHES NI GANG GSUNGS PA,

00:12:33.767 --> 00:12:34.975
,DE NI LUS DANG NGAG GIR YIN,

00:12:34.975 --> 00:12:36.380
You guys can figure this out.

00:12:36.380 --> 00:12:37.860
What is SEMS PA?

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:41.656
It's YID KYI LAS, YID KYI LAS.

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:44.699
Karma of-

00:12:44.699 --> 00:12:45.532
the mind.

00:12:45.532 --> 00:12:47.060
What is BSAMS PA?

00:12:47.060 --> 00:12:49.160
What's the thing you saw?

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:51.491
It's LUS and what?

00:12:51.491 --> 00:12:52.391
- [Woman] Body and speech.

00:12:52.391 --> 00:12:56.080
- Yeah, body and speech,
what you say and what you do.

00:12:56.080 --> 00:12:57.373
Three in a row.

00:12:59.872 --> 00:13:03.511
Something's definitely
going on. I don't know.

00:13:03.511 --> 00:13:04.530
What's the picture?

00:13:04.530 --> 00:13:06.930
Oh, even the picture was boring,

00:13:06.930 --> 00:13:09.363
so I picked a picture from above.

00:13:10.220 --> 00:13:12.180
Wait, yeah I'm sorry, no.

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:15.760
That's from the last one,
that's thinking and thought.

00:13:15.760 --> 00:13:19.920
The balloon is thought,
I'm explaining it to you.

00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:24.216
And here's talking and doing
which comes from thinking.

00:13:25.290 --> 00:13:30.290
All right, let's go try to find
a verse which is challenging.

00:13:30.290 --> 00:13:32.298
Oh, here's one [laughs].

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:37.930
In the next two verses he outlines

00:13:37.930 --> 00:13:39.950
seven types of karma.

00:13:39.950 --> 00:13:43.392
He promised us BYE BRAG,
right, what was that?

00:13:44.268 --> 00:13:45.710
SPYI BYE BRAG

00:13:45.710 --> 00:13:47.719
He promised us,

00:13:47.719 --> 00:13:49.760
he promised us many categories of karma.

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:51.060
Well, here they are.

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:54.870
Here's the easiest one,
and it's intriguing

00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:58.940
what Nagarjuna thinks
is a division of karma

00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:01.100
because if somebody asked me

00:14:01.100 --> 00:14:03.040
what's the different kinds of karma

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:06.620
I would say the 10 good deeds
or the 10 bad deeds, right?

00:14:06.620 --> 00:14:11.210
And he goes off on this weird
thing which is so Nagarjuna.

00:14:11.210 --> 00:14:12.240
Here we go.

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:14.710
Well, NGAG.

00:14:14.710 --> 00:14:17.238
That's easy. Talking.

00:14:17.238 --> 00:14:19.420
NGAG -- talking, all right?

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:21.819
Like NGAG DBANG is a typical Tibetan name

00:14:21.819 --> 00:14:25.966
which means Vagishvara,

00:14:25.966 --> 00:14:28.340
the power of speech.

00:14:28.340 --> 00:14:29.639
So NGAG.

00:14:29.639 --> 00:14:30.923
Then he says BSKYOD PA,

00:14:30.923 --> 00:14:34.262
and you guys know MI
BSKYOD PA -- Akshobhya.

00:14:35.289 --> 00:14:36.340
- [Woman] Unshakable.

00:14:36.340 --> 00:14:38.780
- Yeah, unmoving like a mountain.

00:14:38.780 --> 00:14:40.689
So what's kshobhya?

00:14:40.689 --> 00:14:41.522
[student responding indistinctly]

00:14:41.522 --> 00:14:42.861
Which means?

00:14:42.861 --> 00:14:46.120
[students responding indistinctly]

00:14:46.120 --> 00:14:48.832
Speech and action.

00:14:48.832 --> 00:14:49.940
Physical action.

00:14:49.940 --> 00:14:54.940
It's interesting, he calls it moving.

00:14:55.360 --> 00:14:57.270
Moving your body.

00:14:57.270 --> 00:15:00.912
So how many kinds of karma so far? Two.

00:15:00.912 --> 00:15:02.195
Okay, two.

00:15:05.720 --> 00:15:10.293
Okay, Tim, 200 bucks. From the Abhidharma,

00:15:11.202 --> 00:15:15.202
RNAM RIG and RNAM RIG BYED MA YIN PA

00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:22.810
Two divisions of... think of
weird things in Stanley's text

00:15:22.810 --> 00:15:24.819
that have to do with karma.

00:15:24.819 --> 00:15:25.928
[student responding indistinctly]

00:15:25.928 --> 00:15:30.928
%Darn, $200! Dang!

00:15:31.100 --> 00:15:33.780
Yeah, one is, what's the classic example?

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:35.130
When you take a vow.

00:15:35.130 --> 00:15:36.195
When you get down on your knee

00:15:36.195 --> 00:15:39.600
and you do this chicken posture thing,

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:41.590
anyone can guess your motivation,

00:15:41.590 --> 00:15:43.040
it's MA KHYAB, right?

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:46.369
You could be thinking
about lunch, but [laughs].

00:15:47.320 --> 00:15:51.260
So from the form, someone
can guess your motivation.

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:55.539
Later, according to the
Abhidharma, you have a?

00:15:55.539 --> 00:15:56.450
[student responding indistinctly]

00:15:56.450 --> 00:15:58.720
Like an aura or a halo around you

00:15:58.720 --> 00:16:03.070
which is your vow's influence stays,

00:16:03.070 --> 00:16:04.630
and it's invisible.

00:16:04.630 --> 00:16:09.603
You can go to the bar and you can...

00:16:10.470 --> 00:16:13.453
my translator in Mongolia, it's so cute,

00:16:13.453 --> 00:16:16.080
said, "Geshe-la you ruined my life!"

00:16:16.080 --> 00:16:18.500
The second time I went
there he had a beard

00:16:18.500 --> 00:16:20.103
and I said what's going on?

00:16:20.103 --> 00:16:24.430
He said, "Geshe-la we were on
national TV teaching dharma."

00:16:24.430 --> 00:16:28.446
And I said well yeah, and he says,
"I can't go to the bar anymore."

00:16:28.446 --> 00:16:29.760
[laughter]

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:31.820
Everybody's asking. I had to grow a beard

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:34.280
so they wouldn't recognize me.

00:16:34.280 --> 00:16:37.020
So anyway, why are we talking about that?

00:16:37.020 --> 00:16:39.910
You can't guess from the
bearded guy in the bar

00:16:39.910 --> 00:16:41.680
that he had the karmic aura

00:16:41.680 --> 00:16:45.043
of having taught dharma on national TV.

00:16:46.139 --> 00:16:47.550
NGAG DANG BSKYOD DANG

00:16:47.550 --> 00:16:49.098
Okay, those two are RNAM RIG.

00:16:49.098 --> 00:16:52.365
What's the MA YIN DGAG, Tim?

00:16:54.640 --> 00:16:57.353
If the first two are RNAM RIG...

00:16:57.353 --> 00:16:58.440
[student responding indistinctly]

00:16:58.440 --> 00:17:00.558
Yeah, then the next one's going to be

00:17:00.558 --> 00:17:02.480
RNAM RIG MA YIN, a non-communicating aura.

00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:05.310
Now he's going to talk about the aura.

00:17:05.310 --> 00:17:10.310
So far we got two, we got
speech and physical movement,

00:17:10.890 --> 00:17:15.270
Now we got RNAM RIG MIN.

00:17:15.270 --> 00:17:18.310
And then he calls it MI SPONG BA.

00:17:19.580 --> 00:17:23.160
You don't give up, you don't give up.

00:17:23.160 --> 00:17:26.810
And Choney Lama says that's
Nagarjuna's short hand

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:29.417
for you don't give up MI DGE BA.

00:17:31.111 --> 00:17:32.600
[student responding indistinctly]

00:17:32.600 --> 00:17:34.933
Yeah, so it implies you are?

00:17:35.962 --> 00:17:39.812
If you are MI DGE BA SPONG, you are?

00:17:39.812 --> 00:17:42.807
If you give up MI DGE BA, you are?

00:17:42.807 --> 00:17:44.370
DGE BA, yeah.

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:49.370
So why Nagarjuna calls good
deeds not-giving-up deeds?

00:17:53.150 --> 00:17:56.743
It's because you don't give up bad deeds.

00:17:57.680 --> 00:18:01.170
He defines, he's describing good deeds

00:18:01.170 --> 00:18:04.350
as not-giving-up deeds, but that means

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:07.453
not giving up bad deeds,
which is good deeds.

00:18:09.047 --> 00:18:13.214
[student responding indistinctly]

00:18:14.100 --> 00:18:16.760
I'm sorry, giving up bad deeds.

00:18:16.760 --> 00:18:18.194
Yeah, okay.

00:18:18.194 --> 00:18:21.070
MI SPONG RNAM RIG MIN

00:18:21.070 --> 00:18:24.303
I'm sorry, I screwed that
up, let's do it again.

00:18:24.303 --> 00:18:28.490
MI SPONG BA means, yeah, I'm sorry,

00:18:28.490 --> 00:18:31.190
Yeah, you don't give up bad deeds.

00:18:31.190 --> 00:18:34.180
I said it right the first time.

00:18:34.180 --> 00:18:35.634
Which is?

00:18:35.634 --> 00:18:38.173
- [Woman] MI DGE BA
- A bad deed.

00:18:38.173 --> 00:18:39.310
[student responding indistinctly]

00:18:39.310 --> 00:18:41.140
No, not giving up bad deeds,

00:18:41.140 --> 00:18:44.240
not giving up bad deeds
is a bad deed, that's all.

00:18:44.240 --> 00:18:45.073
Okay, got it?

00:18:45.073 --> 00:18:47.690
So I was right the first time.

00:18:47.690 --> 00:18:50.300
So the category number three

00:18:50.300 --> 00:18:54.960
is not giving up bad
deeds, which is bad deeds.

00:18:54.960 --> 00:18:57.680
But we already covered the non-halo,

00:18:57.680 --> 00:19:02.680
so this must be the halo, which
means the afterglow you get.

00:19:02.957 --> 00:19:06.100
And Choney Lama says
from... and by the way

00:19:06.100 --> 00:19:07.508
this is in the Abhidharma.

00:19:07.508 --> 00:19:10.749
When you joined a trade in ancient India

00:19:10.749 --> 00:19:15.683
you had to take a pledge
to follow that occupation.

00:19:16.816 --> 00:19:21.133
And two famous pledges were
butcher and army, and military.

00:19:22.120 --> 00:19:24.820
I will shoot people, I will kill people.

00:19:24.820 --> 00:19:27.750
That's called a @.

00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:29.644
What's that?

00:19:29.644 --> 00:19:31.552
Anti-vow, it's an anti-vow.

00:19:31.552 --> 00:19:35.593
I promise to follow my father's
trade for the rest of my life.

00:19:35.593 --> 00:19:39.750
My friend in Argentina, her husband is,

00:19:39.750 --> 00:19:42.380
kills the animals in the factory.

00:19:42.380 --> 00:19:45.289
He's always depressed,
they don't know why.

00:19:45.289 --> 00:19:46.560
[laughs] Okay.

00:19:46.560 --> 00:19:51.120
So anyway, so how many we got now?

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:55.960
We got good, we got verbal karma,

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:58.470
action karma which you can see,

00:19:58.470 --> 00:20:02.010
and then we got bad karma, halo,

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:05.300
which is having made a promise to.

00:20:05.300 --> 00:20:09.431
And now we got SPONG BA'I

00:20:09.431 --> 00:20:12.597
where you do give up bad deeds.

00:20:14.260 --> 00:20:18.550
Okay, the halo you get when
you do give up bad deeds,

00:20:18.550 --> 00:20:21.940
And the example of that
halo is the one you get

00:20:21.940 --> 00:20:24.910
after you take your, when
you're just about to take your

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:27.862
medicine buddha initiation?

00:20:27.862 --> 00:20:29.100
You take your Bodhisattva vows.

00:20:29.100 --> 00:20:31.420
So that halo everybody in this class,

00:20:31.420 --> 00:20:36.100
if you took the Nagarjuna's
Bodhisattva vows ceremony,

00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:39.210
you have a halo around you forever.

00:20:39.210 --> 00:20:44.204
Well, yeah. Well, some people
say it stops when you die,

00:20:44.204 --> 00:20:47.450
but not for Bodhisattva vows.

00:20:47.450 --> 00:20:49.700
So two kinds of halos.

00:20:49.700 --> 00:20:54.700
Bad-good halo, talking, doing
that people can interpret,

00:20:56.120 --> 00:20:59.680
and then halos of bad
deeds and good deeds.

00:20:59.680 --> 00:21:01.890
We got four, how many he promised us?

00:21:01.890 --> 00:21:03.260
Seven.

00:21:03.260 --> 00:21:05.060
He promised us seven.

00:21:05.060 --> 00:21:09.094
Why Nagarjuna wants to go
this way, think about it.

00:21:10.540 --> 00:21:12.611
Number five, you okay?

00:21:12.611 --> 00:21:14.870
[student responding indistinctly]

00:21:14.870 --> 00:21:17.867
Yeah, non-communicating is three and four,

00:21:17.867 --> 00:21:20.490
and communicating is one and two.

00:21:20.490 --> 00:21:21.323
Okay, cool.

00:21:21.323 --> 00:21:25.865
We didn't get to the mental ones yet.

00:21:25.865 --> 00:21:28.500
,LONGS SPYOD LAS BYUNG BSOD NAMS DANG,

00:21:28.500 --> 00:21:31.513
Oh, GZHAN DAG KYANG NI
DE BZHIN 'DOD means...

00:21:32.781 --> 00:21:35.850
GZHAN DAG KYANG NI DE BZHIN 'DOD means

00:21:35.850 --> 00:21:39.510
apply that to all the others,
apply that to all the others.

00:21:39.510 --> 00:21:42.613
And he means by that, good or bad.

00:21:43.800 --> 00:21:44.988
Okay? Good or bad.

00:21:44.988 --> 00:21:48.530
When I'm dividing things into good or bad,

00:21:48.530 --> 00:21:52.489
you know, keep doing that
with the rest of them.

00:21:52.489 --> 00:21:56.200
LONGS SPYOD LAS BYUNG BSOD NAMS DANG

00:21:56.200 --> 00:21:58.080
This is interesting.

00:21:59.010 --> 00:22:03.203
Material good deeds
relating to the Dharma.

00:22:04.190 --> 00:22:06.670
Material good deeds
relating to the Dharma.

00:22:06.670 --> 00:22:10.350
Making a donation to save
books with the Gold Club

00:22:10.350 --> 00:22:15.280
or making a donation to build
a stupa for Medicine Buddha.

00:22:15.280 --> 00:22:17.777
And that has a special name in Abhidharma,

00:22:17.777 --> 00:22:21.260
@.

00:22:21.260 --> 00:22:23.278
It's very interesting.

00:22:24.860 --> 00:22:29.860
Like I spent 30 years fixing
the temple in New Jersey,

00:22:30.360 --> 00:22:32.210
the Mongolian monastery.

00:22:32.210 --> 00:22:37.080
I did, I rebuilt many of the
houses and stuff like that.

00:22:37.080 --> 00:22:40.730
And I'm still getting interest on those,

00:22:40.730 --> 00:22:43.020
as long as some monk is
sitting in that house,

00:22:43.020 --> 00:22:44.910
I'm getting interest, karmic interest.

00:22:44.910 --> 00:22:46.530
That's called @.

00:22:46.530 --> 00:22:49.090
So what is number five?

00:22:49.090 --> 00:22:51.970
It's, Nagarjuna thinks it's important

00:22:51.970 --> 00:22:56.228
to isolate this special karma you get

00:22:56.228 --> 00:23:01.228
from physical donations or
contributions to the Dharma,

00:23:02.320 --> 00:23:05.910
which will outlive you
or which will outlive

00:23:05.910 --> 00:23:10.300
your current participation
after you quit the Gold Club.

00:23:10.300 --> 00:23:12.910
If the Gold Club saved a lot of books,

00:23:12.910 --> 00:23:16.360
then every time Geshe-la
uses that book in a class,

00:23:16.360 --> 00:23:18.780
you're still getting karmic interest.

00:23:18.780 --> 00:23:19.613
It's cool.

00:23:19.613 --> 00:23:21.030
Now, for some reason, Nagarjuna thinks

00:23:21.030 --> 00:23:23.503
it's important to separate that one out.

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:27.975
So that could be a whole conversation

00:23:27.975 --> 00:23:30.880
in a study group or something.

00:23:30.880 --> 00:23:34.930
All right, which means that the
Medicine Buddha stupa project

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:39.200
and saving the books project
are interesting projects

00:23:39.200 --> 00:23:41.520
because you keep getting
interest out of them,

00:23:41.520 --> 00:23:45.453
even if you quit the group, you
still get the interest of it.

00:23:45.453 --> 00:23:47.110
All right, cool.

00:23:47.110 --> 00:23:49.240
I'm still getting interest from all the...

00:23:49.240 --> 00:23:51.940
like I built a water system in Sera May.

00:23:51.940 --> 00:23:53.680
So every time some monk takes a drink,

00:23:53.680 --> 00:23:56.650
I'm like getting more karma.

00:23:56.650 --> 00:24:00.700
All right, BSOD NAMS MA YIN TSUL DE BZHIN.

00:24:00.700 --> 00:24:02.880
The same applies to the opposite,

00:24:02.880 --> 00:24:05.770
and Choney Lama says building a facility

00:24:05.770 --> 00:24:09.060
for killing cows would be an example.

00:24:09.060 --> 00:24:11.990
If you build it and then
they keep killing cows there,

00:24:11.990 --> 00:24:13.770
you keep getting karmic interest.

00:24:13.770 --> 00:24:15.630
That's six, we've done six.

00:24:15.630 --> 00:24:18.695
What's number seven going to be?

00:24:18.695 --> 00:24:21.150
SEMS PA

00:24:21.150 --> 00:24:25.110
The pre-intent, the pre-intent.

00:24:25.110 --> 00:24:28.100
Like what was your intention
before you did those six?

00:24:28.100 --> 00:24:31.060
What were you hoping
would be accomplished?

00:24:31.060 --> 00:24:32.690
Good or bad.

00:24:32.690 --> 00:24:34.450
But he puts them
together, so that's seven.

00:24:34.450 --> 00:24:38.304
So we don't get an equal number
because he puts some together.

00:24:38.304 --> 00:24:40.850
Okay, LAS SU MNGON PAR 'DOD PA YIN.

00:24:40.850 --> 00:24:43.115
Somebody super accepts that,

00:24:43.115 --> 00:24:44.650
@

00:24:44.650 --> 00:24:45.483
Who?

00:24:45.483 --> 00:24:47.290
The Buddha.

00:24:47.290 --> 00:24:50.620
Those are the divisions
to what he first described

00:24:50.620 --> 00:24:53.488
as only two, SEMS PA and BSAM PA.

00:24:54.333 --> 00:24:57.865
Chetana and chetayitva.

00:24:57.865 --> 00:25:00.430
Now, you've got seven.

00:25:00.430 --> 00:25:02.430
Any difficult verse yet?

00:25:03.725 --> 00:25:05.420
I think he's going to kick us in the butt,

00:25:05.420 --> 00:25:07.160
I think something's coming.

00:25:07.160 --> 00:25:09.000
I'm just guessing.

00:25:09.000 --> 00:25:12.690
There's a picture, try to
find a picture of these seven.

00:25:12.690 --> 00:25:14.820
Good luck.

00:25:14.820 --> 00:25:18.054
I was thinking, you know, good
and bad karma or something?

00:25:18.054 --> 00:25:19.340
I don't know.

00:25:19.340 --> 00:25:22.307
Anyway, let's skip on.

00:25:25.644 --> 00:25:28.010
GAL TE SMIN PA'I DUS BAR DU

00:25:28.010 --> 00:25:33.010
Now, finally, ha-ha, why did he set us up

00:25:34.520 --> 00:25:39.520
with this calm, understandable,
discussion of karma?

00:25:40.260 --> 00:25:43.507
Because this was coming.

00:25:43.507 --> 00:25:45.949
,GAL TE SMIN PA'I DUS BAR DU,

00:25:45.949 --> 00:25:48.341
,GNAS NA LAS DE RTAG PAR 'GYUR,

00:25:48.341 --> 00:25:52.416
,GAL TE 'GAGS NA 'GAGS GYUR PA,

00:25:52.416 --> 00:25:54.420
,JI LTAR 'BRAS BU SKYE PAR 'GYUR,

00:25:54.420 --> 00:25:57.220
Now he's like, here's Nagarjuna like,

00:25:57.220 --> 00:26:00.063
"Wow, so we did all these kinds of karma,

00:26:00.900 --> 00:26:03.710
well what happens after that?"

00:26:03.710 --> 00:26:06.960
What do you think happens after that?

00:26:06.960 --> 00:26:10.053
Where does the karma stay until it ripens?

00:26:11.000 --> 00:26:15.820
And now, he was setting us
up for three verses, right?

00:26:15.820 --> 00:26:18.280
Five verses.

00:26:18.280 --> 00:26:19.980
He was setting us up.

00:26:19.980 --> 00:26:22.610
And now he asks this innocent question,

00:26:22.610 --> 00:26:27.610
"Oh, where does the karma
stay until it ripens?"

00:26:27.680 --> 00:26:31.203
And then he's like, two possibilities:

00:26:32.900 --> 00:26:37.900
if it stays somewhere
inert until it comes out,

00:26:39.710 --> 00:26:40.850
well then it's RTAG PA,

00:26:40.850 --> 00:26:44.133
it's unchanging, during that period.

00:26:45.100 --> 00:26:48.790
It has to replicate itself as the same,

00:26:48.790 --> 00:26:53.370
it has to clone itself from
year to year until it ripens.

00:26:53.370 --> 00:26:55.420
So that's unchanging, that's RTAG PA,

00:26:55.420 --> 00:26:58.150
and that's impossible
for a functional thing.

00:26:58.150 --> 00:27:02.390
No functional entity in the
universe can not change,

00:27:02.390 --> 00:27:05.830
even for one minute, forget
12 lifetimes or something.

00:27:05.830 --> 00:27:07.510
Not possible.

00:27:07.510 --> 00:27:10.410
So can we, here's Nagarjuna,

00:27:10.410 --> 00:27:13.250
"Can we cancel the first possibility

00:27:13.250 --> 00:27:16.671
that it sits there in
your brain not changing?"

00:27:17.890 --> 00:27:19.600
Yeah, it has to change.

00:27:19.600 --> 00:27:20.990
If it's a functional thing it changes.

00:27:20.990 --> 00:27:22.130
Why?

00:27:22.130 --> 00:27:23.810
Because it's pushed by a cause

00:27:23.810 --> 00:27:28.470
and that energy starts to slow
down as it goes through time.

00:27:30.280 --> 00:27:34.630
Now, oh Geshe-la, you're
saying the longer a karma

00:27:34.630 --> 00:27:38.385
stays in your mind the
less strong it gets?

00:27:39.395 --> 00:27:40.800
[students laughing]

00:27:40.800 --> 00:27:43.056
Okay, well here's the other choice.

00:27:43.056 --> 00:27:45.206
GAL TE 'GAGS NA 'GAGS GYUR PA'I

00:27:45.206 --> 00:27:46.972
JI LTAR 'BRAS BU SKYE PAR 'GYUR,

00:27:46.972 --> 00:27:50.730
If you say it's not
unchanging, then it stops,

00:27:50.730 --> 00:27:54.563
and we don't have to experience
the result of the karma, yay!

00:27:57.312 --> 00:28:02.130
Does it replicate or does it stop?

00:28:02.130 --> 00:28:04.670
It can't replicate because
then it would stay the same

00:28:04.670 --> 00:28:06.770
and it's a functioning thing,

00:28:06.770 --> 00:28:08.090
and it can't stop or else

00:28:08.090 --> 00:28:10.410
all the laws of karma would be broken.

00:28:10.410 --> 00:28:13.170
If it stops all the laws
of karma would be broken.

00:28:13.170 --> 00:28:14.565
You could do whatever you want

00:28:14.565 --> 00:28:18.250
and hope that the karma
stops before it opens.

00:28:18.250 --> 00:28:19.083
Okay?

00:28:20.800 --> 00:28:23.133
Did you ever think about it? No.

00:28:24.050 --> 00:28:28.242
Okay, somebody tell me why
the next picture is relevant.

00:28:33.190 --> 00:28:36.324
Did you ever apply for
a job in New York or LA?

00:28:36.324 --> 00:28:37.474
I'm asking my [laughs],

00:28:39.230 --> 00:28:41.833
you spent hours in waiting rooms, right?

00:28:41.833 --> 00:28:45.418
Were you the same person who
went into the waiting room?

00:28:45.418 --> 00:28:47.767
I mean, to me your karma is like,

00:28:47.767 --> 00:28:50.220
goes in the writing room and
then finally some one says

00:28:50.220 --> 00:28:51.757
okay I am interviewing you.

00:28:51.757 --> 00:28:53.235
You know what they always say?

00:28:53.235 --> 00:28:55.935
They say, "Oh it's five o'clock,
can you come back tomorrow?"

00:28:55.935 --> 00:28:57.361
You say, "I've been here
since three o'clock."

00:28:57.361 --> 00:28:58.953
They say yeah but...

00:29:00.440 --> 00:29:04.780
That's called applying for a
job in New York or LA, right?

00:29:04.780 --> 00:29:06.601
Okay, you know.

00:29:08.080 --> 00:29:10.303
All right, next verse.

00:29:11.440 --> 00:29:13.440
And by the way, the final two verses

00:29:13.440 --> 00:29:16.340
of what I chose for this class,

00:29:16.340 --> 00:29:18.950
and we'll continue in the next class,

00:29:18.950 --> 00:29:21.458
because this is a long chapter.

00:29:22.383 --> 00:29:27.383
Two lower schools come and
try to explain the question.

00:29:27.890 --> 00:29:31.511
So I assume some bigger
school's going to come later,

00:29:31.511 --> 00:29:34.042
I don't know, I didn't read ahead.

00:29:34.042 --> 00:29:39.042
But here's the answer of the MDO SDE PA,

00:29:39.780 --> 00:29:43.720
the Sutra school, second school,

00:29:43.720 --> 00:29:46.662
and the, what do you call that?

00:29:46.662 --> 00:29:48.800
KHA CHE, KHA CHE

00:29:48.800 --> 00:29:52.830
which means Kashmiris,
the guys from Kashmir.

00:29:54.000 --> 00:29:55.570
Which means an Abhidharma school

00:29:55.570 --> 00:29:57.880
that used to hang out in northern India.

00:29:57.880 --> 00:30:01.400
Later, that area became Muslim,

00:30:01.400 --> 00:30:05.513
and now the Tibetan word
for Muslim is Kashmiri.

00:30:06.369 --> 00:30:08.027
KHA CHEs, same word.

00:30:08.027 --> 00:30:09.860
Like @, right?

00:30:09.860 --> 00:30:12.584
Okay, here we go.

00:30:12.584 --> 00:30:14.734
,MYU GU LA SOGS RGYUN GANG NI,

00:30:14.734 --> 00:30:16.441
,SA BON LAS NI MNGON PAR 'BYUNG,

00:30:16.441 --> 00:30:18.216
,DE LAS 'BRAS BU SA BON NI,

00:30:18.216 --> 00:30:20.883
,MED NA DE YANG 'BYUNG MI 'GYUR,

00:30:22.330 --> 00:30:23.460
First you have the seed.

00:30:23.460 --> 00:30:26.390
By the way, who's this? Lower Buddhists.

00:30:26.390 --> 00:30:29.690
Well, first you have,
they're answering Nagarjuna,

00:30:29.690 --> 00:30:31.885
"First you have the seed."

00:30:33.000 --> 00:30:35.310
MYU GU LA SOGS RGYUN GANG YIN

00:30:35.310 --> 00:30:38.463
And then it opens and there's a flow.

00:30:39.910 --> 00:30:42.350
Sorry, before it opens.

00:30:42.350 --> 00:30:44.190
First you have the seed,

00:30:44.190 --> 00:30:47.225
and then something comes
out which is a flow.

00:30:48.596 --> 00:30:52.376
Here's the seed, the flow
comes and breaks out,

00:30:53.476 --> 00:30:57.173
and then it ripens, so no problem.

00:30:58.200 --> 00:31:01.110
It's not that the seed
is repeating itself,

00:31:01.110 --> 00:31:03.500
which would be unchanging,
which is impossible.

00:31:03.500 --> 00:31:05.200
The seed produces something right away,

00:31:05.200 --> 00:31:08.520
it's called the flow of the karma.

00:31:08.520 --> 00:31:11.873
Here's the seed, karma opens, comes out.

00:31:13.000 --> 00:31:15.427
Wait, boop, [vocalizing].

00:31:18.220 --> 00:31:20.800
Okay, and that's the
ripening of the karma.

00:31:20.800 --> 00:31:22.670
So no problem.

00:31:22.670 --> 00:31:24.750
- Does the seed ripen
into the karma right away?

00:31:24.750 --> 00:31:27.070
- No, it flows.

00:31:27.070 --> 00:31:28.140
- And then what happens?

00:31:28.140 --> 00:31:30.970
- At the end of the flow
it opens into the result.

00:31:30.970 --> 00:31:31.860
Got it?

00:31:31.860 --> 00:31:33.910
Therefore, no problem.

00:31:33.910 --> 00:31:36.880
It's still changing because it's flowing,

00:31:36.880 --> 00:31:39.960
but the karmic result hasn't opened yet.

00:31:39.960 --> 00:31:41.626
Got it? No problem.

00:31:41.626 --> 00:31:44.250
Seed, flow, result.

00:31:44.250 --> 00:31:47.200
Seed, flow, result.

00:31:47.200 --> 00:31:48.540
Got it?

00:31:48.540 --> 00:31:51.464
That's the lower Buddhist school.

00:31:51.464 --> 00:31:56.050
DE LAS 'BRAS BU SA BON NI

00:31:56.050 --> 00:31:58.287
And then comes the result.

00:31:58.287 --> 00:32:01.010
MED NA DE YANG 'BYUNG MI 'GYUR

00:32:01.010 --> 00:32:05.153
The result could not have
happened without the seed first,

00:32:06.120 --> 00:32:08.870
therefore the result is
connected to the seed.

00:32:08.870 --> 00:32:10.400
If the seed had never happened,

00:32:10.400 --> 00:32:12.170
the result, at the end of the flow,

00:32:12.170 --> 00:32:13.570
never would've come out.

00:32:13.570 --> 00:32:16.490
Therefore the seed is causing the result,

00:32:16.490 --> 00:32:19.530
but via a flow.

00:32:19.530 --> 00:32:21.810
So they get out of the question

00:32:21.810 --> 00:32:23.797
that the seed didn't cause the result.

00:32:23.797 --> 00:32:28.150
The seed came before the
result, it did cause the result,

00:32:28.150 --> 00:32:31.560
it just took awhile and it was flowing.

00:32:31.560 --> 00:32:33.443
That's their thing.

00:32:33.443 --> 00:32:35.650
GANG PHYIR SA BON LAS RGYUN DANG

00:32:35.650 --> 00:32:37.620
How does that work again?

00:32:37.620 --> 00:32:40.060
There's a SA BON, there's a seed,

00:32:40.060 --> 00:32:42.400
then there's a flow, RGYUN,

00:32:42.400 --> 00:32:44.850
and then RGYUN LAS 'BRAS BU.

00:32:44.850 --> 00:32:47.840
Then the flow turns into the result.

00:32:47.840 --> 00:32:52.840
And because the seed
must predate the result,

00:32:53.660 --> 00:32:57.210
we avoid your two extremes.

00:32:57.210 --> 00:32:59.780
We avoid your two extremes

00:32:59.780 --> 00:33:03.400
which is another version of
the two husbands extremes,

00:33:03.400 --> 00:33:06.880
which is a more simple version
of the two husbands extremes,

00:33:06.880 --> 00:33:11.220
which means does the seed ever stop,

00:33:11.220 --> 00:33:15.090
or does the seed go on unchanging?

00:33:15.090 --> 00:33:16.720
Both of those are extremes.

00:33:16.720 --> 00:33:17.790
Why?

00:33:17.790 --> 00:33:21.530
If the seed shut down
before the result came out

00:33:21.530 --> 00:33:23.270
there'd never be a result.

00:33:23.270 --> 00:33:25.550
If the seed kept going on the same way

00:33:25.550 --> 00:33:29.340
until the result came out,
that would be unchanging,

00:33:29.340 --> 00:33:31.800
and that's not possible
for a functional thing.

00:33:31.800 --> 00:33:36.800
So just, it's just the flow,
man, stay with the flow.

00:33:37.006 --> 00:33:40.206
[laughs] Okay?

00:33:40.206 --> 00:33:42.523
Who is that lower school, all right?

00:33:45.930 --> 00:33:48.192
By the way, then the Nagarjuna's like,

00:33:48.192 --> 00:33:50.120
Nagarjuna, you know,
everybody's looking at

00:33:50.120 --> 00:33:55.120
these lower Buddhist
guys like this, you know?

00:33:55.332 --> 00:33:56.165
Huh?

00:33:56.165 --> 00:34:00.270
And they say, "Oh let's explain,
let us explain further."

00:34:00.270 --> 00:34:03.760
Which usually means digging
a deeper hole for themselves.

00:34:03.760 --> 00:34:06.210
You know, Nagarjuna's like what?

00:34:06.210 --> 00:34:09.010
And they're like the next two verses is,

00:34:09.010 --> 00:34:13.177
the next two verses is their
clarification of their position.

00:34:14.320 --> 00:34:17.490
By the way, if you don't have
Choney Lama you don't know that.

00:34:17.490 --> 00:34:19.352
It sounds like Nagarjuna.

00:34:19.352 --> 00:34:24.352
So anyway, @'GYUR.

00:34:24.960 --> 00:34:28.314
Okay, the flow of the
mind comes from the mind.

00:34:28.314 --> 00:34:30.210
DE LAS 'BRAS BU

00:34:30.210 --> 00:34:32.343
And then that turns into the result.

00:34:36.870 --> 00:34:39.520
The mind begets a mental flow,

00:34:39.520 --> 00:34:42.030
and then the mental flow
turns into the result.

00:34:42.030 --> 00:34:43.556
Three steps.

00:34:45.281 --> 00:34:47.600
DE LAS 'BRAS BU.

00:34:47.600 --> 00:34:50.161
BUS, he uses instrumental, B-U-S.

00:34:50.161 --> 00:34:52.170
BUS, which means therefore,

00:34:52.170 --> 00:34:55.600
the other guy is drawing a conclusion.

00:34:55.600 --> 00:34:58.950
Because there's a mind and
because then the flow of the mind

00:34:58.950 --> 00:35:01.572
and then the result comes, but therefore

00:35:01.572 --> 00:35:04.692
@SEMS.

00:35:04.692 --> 00:35:07.071
@SEMS means,

00:35:07.071 --> 00:35:10.540
it's an idiomatic expression which means

00:35:11.570 --> 00:35:14.911
forget it without the mind,
you got to have the mind,

00:35:14.911 --> 00:35:17.480
@SEMS means forget it if there's no mind.

00:35:17.480 --> 00:35:18.313
- There has to be a mind.

00:35:18.313 --> 00:35:19.146
- Why?

00:35:19.146 --> 00:35:22.430
- I just told you: mind, flow, result.

00:35:22.430 --> 00:35:23.760
Don't tell me you can't have a mind

00:35:23.760 --> 00:35:25.740
at the beginning of that.

00:35:25.740 --> 00:35:27.069
Without that, nothing.

00:35:27.069 --> 00:35:27.902
@SEMS means

00:35:27.902 --> 00:35:31.151
you can't dump the mind, you
got to have the mind there.

00:35:31.151 --> 00:35:33.412
@ means, you know,

00:35:33.412 --> 00:35:36.359
what the heck without the mind.

00:35:36.359 --> 00:35:39.200
@SEMS... MED NA

00:35:39.200 --> 00:35:42.290
If the mind wasn't there, 'BYUNG MI 'GYUR,

00:35:42.290 --> 00:35:44.070
the whole process would never happen.

00:35:44.070 --> 00:35:48.720
It has to start with
mind, then mind flows.

00:35:48.720 --> 00:35:51.780
If you say the flow of the
mind is not part of the process

00:35:51.780 --> 00:35:53.282
then how could you have a karma

00:35:53.282 --> 00:35:56.310
if you didn't have any thinking.

00:35:56.310 --> 00:35:57.787
He's like,

00:35:58.900 --> 00:36:01.910
what do you call it [indistinct]?

00:36:01.910 --> 00:36:04.130
[student responding indistinctly]

00:36:04.130 --> 00:36:05.094
Logical-

00:36:05.094 --> 00:36:07.510
[student responding indistinctly]

00:36:07.510 --> 00:36:11.020
You're switching terms.

00:36:11.020 --> 00:36:13.600
- Anyway, it has to start with the mind.

00:36:13.600 --> 00:36:14.433
- Why?

00:36:14.433 --> 00:36:15.870
- Karma starts with the mind.

00:36:15.870 --> 00:36:17.010
- Are you telling me there's no mind?

00:36:17.010 --> 00:36:18.240
- No, no, no, there's mind.

00:36:18.240 --> 00:36:19.073
- Why?

00:36:19.073 --> 00:36:20.220
- Mind is the base of karma.

00:36:20.220 --> 00:36:22.681
- Okay, so it's flowing, what
do you have a problem with that?

00:36:22.681 --> 00:36:25.885
[laughs] That's all he's saying.

00:36:25.885 --> 00:36:28.730
You never could've had a karmic
result without a mind anyway,

00:36:28.730 --> 00:36:32.220
so don't tell me my theory
is wrong that there's a flow

00:36:32.220 --> 00:36:34.350
because the flow happens
to be the flow of the mind,

00:36:34.350 --> 00:36:37.180
which you agree has to be
there at the beginning.

00:36:37.180 --> 00:36:38.373
Got it?

00:36:38.373 --> 00:36:39.402
Okay.

00:36:39.402 --> 00:36:41.160
%GANG PHYIR SA BON LAS RGYUN DANG NI

00:36:41.160 --> 00:36:42.689
RGYUN LAS 'BRAS BU 'BYUNG 'GYUR ZHING

00:36:42.689 --> 00:36:46.930
I just told you the
flow comes from the mind

00:36:46.930 --> 00:36:48.700
and then the mind keeps flowing,

00:36:48.700 --> 00:36:50.010
and then at the end of the flow

00:36:50.010 --> 00:36:53.224
you get a 'BRAS BU, you get a result.

00:36:53.224 --> 00:36:54.723
LAS NI 'BRAS BU'I SNGON 'GRO BA

00:36:54.723 --> 00:36:56.778
DE PHYIR CHAD MIN RTAG MA YIN

00:36:56.778 --> 00:37:01.340
And because the planting
of the karma in the mind

00:37:01.340 --> 00:37:06.340
has to predate the result,
I avoid your problems,

00:37:06.360 --> 00:37:08.500
the two problems that you suggested.

00:37:08.500 --> 00:37:10.410
What were the two problems we suggested?

00:37:10.410 --> 00:37:12.950
Number one that the karmic seed

00:37:15.480 --> 00:37:19.130
would keep replicating
itself, unchangedly,

00:37:19.130 --> 00:37:23.433
or that it would just,
what do you call that?

00:37:25.100 --> 00:37:27.990
Truncate.

00:37:27.990 --> 00:37:28.823
Got it?

00:37:28.823 --> 00:37:32.185
That's a perfect word
actually, write that down.

00:37:32.185 --> 00:37:36.470
All right, we finished the
first half of that chapter.

00:37:36.470 --> 00:37:40.520
We will continue with
deep dive class number 13

00:37:40.520 --> 00:37:41.353
in the next lesson.

00:37:41.353 --> 00:37:43.386
Let's summarize.

00:37:44.294 --> 00:37:49.000
Nagarjuna set us up with
some understandable stuff

00:37:49.000 --> 00:37:50.980
at the beginning, right?

00:37:50.980 --> 00:37:53.520
What is karma? Thinking

00:37:53.520 --> 00:37:57.500
and then the actions motivated
by thinking and speech.

00:37:57.500 --> 00:37:59.580
And then he got into
seven different kinds,

00:37:59.580 --> 00:38:04.080
which included the halo stuff

00:38:04.080 --> 00:38:07.471
and emphasized,

00:38:07.471 --> 00:38:12.471
had a noticeable bias

00:38:12.720 --> 00:38:15.830
towards physical Dharma actions,

00:38:15.830 --> 00:38:20.410
supporting physical,
like the input project.

00:38:20.410 --> 00:38:24.980
And then he went on to
discuss whether or not what?

00:38:24.980 --> 00:38:28.710
How does the seed stay in mind?

00:38:28.710 --> 00:38:30.760
If it doesn't change there's a problem,

00:38:30.760 --> 00:38:33.800
if it does stop there's a problem.

00:38:33.800 --> 00:38:38.320
And then we had an attempted
explanation by some guys

00:38:38.320 --> 00:38:40.690
who keep talking about
some kind of flow thing

00:38:40.690 --> 00:38:44.310
that connects the result
to the original seed

00:38:44.310 --> 00:38:47.438
without the seed changing or stopping.

00:38:48.600 --> 00:38:49.850
Cool?

00:38:49.850 --> 00:38:52.591
All right, see you next class.

